ick Science Education Center School of Business Administration School of Education School of Nursing Sociology Staff Assembly Student Affairs Student Health Center Student Organizations Student Publications Student Success Center Technology Services Technology Services Help Desk Title IX News and Information University Policies USC Integrity Line USCA LIFE Veteran & Military Student Success Visual & Performing Arts Wellness Center & Natatorium Workforce Development & Innovation Writing Center Career Services Career Services Home Departments ›  Career Services Students Career Planning & Exploration College to Career ASUP 410 Experiential Education Individual Appointments Job Search Additional Job Search Links Printable Resources Remote Employment Student Employment Employer Partners Hiring International Students Faculty Parents and Families Career Planning Frequently Asked Questions Events and Programs Career Fairs Graduate Outcomes 2022-2023 2023-2024 Handshake Hub Handshake for Students Handshake for Employers Handshake for Faculty and Staff Career development is integral to university life and provides students and alumni with the guidance, knowledge, experiences, skills, and connections that will lead to successful, lifelong career management. To fully take advantage of the many resources and services available, students must take some initiative. In this rapidly changing, competitive global market, the Career Services staff invites students to empower themselves by taking charge of their career futures. The staff is available to assist students through this process. Students can begin taking charge of their futures by applying for job positions and internships in the community. Many job openings are posted on Handshake , USCA’s online job board. Career Services can also assist alumni in their search for full-time employment. Individual career counseling appointments are available upon request. Career Services also assists with career preparation through initiatives such as career panels, the Leadership USCA program, and the College To Career Readiness (C2CR) program. For Students Student Services Career Fairs Career Planning & Exploration College To Career ASUP 410 Events Calendar Experiential Education Individual Appointments Handshake for Students Job Search Leadership USCA Printable Resources Remote Employment Student Employment Additional Job Search Links For Employers Handshake for Employers Career Fairs Events Calendar Hiring International Students For Parents & Families Parents & Families Career Planning Frequently Asked Questions Location Penland 108 Phone Call  at 803-641-3440 Email CareerServices@usca.edu Contact Us Director Corey Feraldi Call Corey Feraldi at Administrative Assistant Mary Clark Call Mary Clark at Department Directory Quick Links Handshake Hub About Academics Admissions Athletics Departments Student Affairs Research & Grants © 2024-2025\r\n        University of South Carolina Aiken Jobs • Title IX • Integrity Line • Giving • Website • Accessibility • Privacy TOP"
