      "description": "Dean of Students | USCA Skip to Content 1 Site alerts Menu Search × Search Search: All USCA Faculty & Staff Programs Search USCA Browse All USCA.edu Filter browse results Loading A-to-Z... MENU Academics Program Search College of Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences Communication and Emerging Media English and Writing Languages, Literatures and Cultures History, Political Science and Philosophy Sociology Visual and Performing Arts College of Sciences and Engineering Biological, Environmental and Earth Sciences Chemistry and Physics Exercise and Sports Science Computer Science, Engineering and Mathematics Psychology School of Business Administration School of Education School of Nursing Admissions Request Information Tuition & Fees Visit Campus Apply Online Athletics Departments Academic Affairs Admissions Aiken County Commission for Higher Education Aiken Partnership Board Alumni Relations Athletics Behavioral Intervention Team Bookstore Broken Ink Budget Office Business Services Callen Center for Engaged Teaching and Learning Campus Auxiliary & Support Services Campus Recreation And Wellness Campus Safety & University Police Career Services Children's Center Counseling Center Dean of Students Development and Alumni Affairs Dining Services Disability Services Enrollment Management & Marketing Equestrian Club Sports Esports Etherredge Center External Programs Facility Rentals Financial Aid First Year Experience Giving Graduation Greek Life Gregg-Graniteville Library Honors Housing Human Resources Innovation Hub Institutional Effectiveness, Research & Compliance International Programs Judicial Affairs Multimedia Services Marketing and Communication News and Information Off the Shelf Office of the Chancellor Online Learning & Support Operations Palmetto College Parent & Family Relations Regional Security Operations Center Registrar Research and Grants Ruth Patrick Science Education Center Staff Assembly Student Affairs Student Health Center Student Organizations Student Publications Student Success Center Technology Services Technology Services Help Desk Title IX University Policies USCA LIFE Veteran & Military Student Success Wellness Center & Natatorium Workforce Development & Innovation Writing Center Student Affairs Research and Grants INFORMATION FOR Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Families Military Community Request Info Visit Apply Give Tuition and Fees About USCA Academic Affairs Academic Bulletins Academic Calendars Academic Curricular Enrichment (ACE) Academics (Colleges & Schools) Accolades Accreditation Admissions Aiken County Commission for Higher Education Aiken Online Aiken Partnership Board Alumni Relations Athletics Behavioral Intervention Team Bookstore Broken Ink Budget Office Business Services Callen Center for Engaged Teaching and Learning Campus Auxiliary & Support Services Campus Calendar Campus Map & Directions Campus Recreation And Wellness Campus Safety & University Police Career Services Children's Center College of Arts, Humanities & Social Sciences College of Sciences & Engineering Communication & Emerging Media Counseling Center Dean of Students Departments (Non-Academic) Department Directory Development and Alumni Affairs Dining Services Disability Services English Enrollment Management & Marketing Equestrian Club Sports Esports Etherredge Center External Programs Facility Rentals Faculty Manual Financial Aid First Year Experience Giving Graduation Greek Life Gregg-Graniteville Library History, Political Science & Philosophy Honors Housing Human Resources Innovation Hub Institutional Effectiveness, Research & Compliance International Programs Judicial Affairs Languages, Literatures & Cultures Math Lab Multimedia Services MyUSCA Marketing and Communication Off the Shelf Office of the Chancellor Online Learning & Support Operations Palmetto College Parent & Family Relations People Directory Programs Search Regional Security Operations Center Registrar Research and Grants Ruth Patrick Science Education Center School of Business Administration School of Education School of Nursing Sociology Staff Assembly Student Affairs Student Health Center Student Organizations Student Publications Student Success Center Technology Services Technology Services Help Desk Title IX News and Information University Policies USC Integrity Line USCA LIFE Veteran & Military Student Success Visual & Performing Arts Wellness Center & Natatorium Workforce Development & Innovation Writing Center Dean of Students Dean of Students Home Departments › Student Affairs ›  Dean of Students Mission Statement and Values Resources Freedom of Expression on Campus Free Speech on Campus Hazing Student Code of Conduct Title IX and Sexual Misconduct AIM Mentor Program Community Concerns Response Team Directory Welcome The Office of the Dean of Students is available to assist students, faculty, staff, and community members, promoting the holistic development of students, focusing on student advocacy, crisis management, and personal accountability. The office is located in the Student Life Suite in the Student Activity Center (488 Scholars Loop, Aiken, SC 29801). The Dean of Students is available to support students through situations that impact their access to a high-quality student experience. The Office of the DOS will work directly with students on a variety of issues including, but not limited to: Academic Support Financial Concerns Campus Climate Concerns On and Off Campus Concerns Referrals to Health, Safety and Wellbeing Resources Dear Pacers, Whether you are a continuing student or a new student, you are an integral part of our campus community. Serving as the Dean of Students for the University of South Carolina Aiken is an honor and a privilege. As a proud graduate of this university, I stand elated to ensure that every student at the university feels that they belong at USCA, while ensure to maintain the culture of respect that has come to be a fixture in the identity of this university. My role is to assist all students with navigating tough situations that many college students go through, help maintain a safe environment for all students and ensure that you receive the tools to maximize your student experience. I am here to be a listening ear and connect to students to campus and community resources that will help them thrive and be successful as a student, here, at the University of South Carolina Aiken. Please reach out to me at any time if I can aid you during your academic journey. GO PACERS!!! Dr. Jamel Hodges ‘11 Dean of Students How to Request Support from the DOS By Phone : Call the Office of the Dean of Students at (803) 641-3442 during normal business hours (Monday – Thursday, 8:00am – 5:00pm; Friday, 8:00am – 12:30pm). If it is after business hours, please leave a voicemail. By Email : Email the Office of the Dean of Students at dos@usca.edu . You will receive a reply no later than 48 hours after the email is received. By Drop-In : You can come into the office during normal business hours to speak with the DOS. Online : You can submit an Incident Reporting Form to report time-sensitive requests that requires the attention of the DOS and other campus entities. Submissions are reviewed when University offices are open. *This will depend on the availability of the DOS. Location SAC 161 Phone Call  at 803-641-3442 Contact Us Dean of Students Dr. Jamel Hodges Call Dr. Jamel Hodges at Department Directory About Academics Admissions Athletics Departments Student Affairs Research & Grants © 2024-2025\r\n        University of South Carolina Aiken Jobs • Title IX • Integrity Line • Giving • Website • Accessibility • Privacy TOP"
