Ruth Patrick Science Education Center School of Business Administration School of Education School of Nursing Sociology Staff Assembly Student Affairs Student Health Center Student Organizations Student Publications Student Success Center Technology Services Technology Services Help Desk Title IX News and Information University Policies USC Integrity Line USCA LIFE Veteran & Military Student Success Visual & Performing Arts Wellness Center & Natatorium Workforce Development & Innovation Writing Center Employment Opportunities Human Resources Home Departments › Human Resources ›  Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities Faculty Recruitment Guide Student Hires Current Job Openings Resources Benefits Frequently Asked Questions Holidays Forms Payroll Information HR System Links Training Workshop Schedule Workers' Compensation USC Integrity Line HR Policies Directory Current Job Openings All positions have to be applied for online. Paper applications will not be accepted. VIEW OPEN POSITIONS ADDITIONAL TEMPORARY POSITIONS About USCA The University of South Carolina Aiken (USCA), a public comprehensive university in the University of South Carolina system, offers undergraduate and master’s degrees to more than 4000 students in 60 programs of study. USCA has ranked as one of the best public schools in the South by U.S. News & World Report for the 26th year in a row. Additionally, USCA was recognized for being a Best College for Veterans and a Top Performer in Social Mobility. USCA is South Carolina’s COPLAC institution providing a unique and strong liberal arts core within our degree offerings. We boast students from 35 states and 32 countries. USCA has ten NCAA Division II Athletic programs. Situated on 450 acres, USCA is located thirty minutes from Augusta, GA (home of the Masters Tournament and Fort Gordon, new home of US Army Cyber Command), one hour from Columbia, SC, and within three hours of Charleston, SC, coastal beaches, and the Appalachian Mountains. Aiken is noted for its famous thoroughbred horses, numerous parks and golf courses, wonderful weather, spacious avenues, and historic homes. USCA does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Learn More About USCA Location B&E 257 Phone Call  at 803-641-3644 Email HR@usca.edu Fax 803-641-3693 Contact Us Director Carla Hayes Call Carla Hayes at Administrative Assistant Jenni Zollinger Call Jenni Zollinger at Department Directory About Academics Admissions Athletics Departments Student Affairs Research & Grants © 2024-2026\r\n        University of South Carolina Aiken Jobs • Title IX • Integrity Line • Giving • Website • Accessibility • Privacy TOP"
